{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ELPvBGVkxL9ttywtpbyAkX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier definition. Let me identify all planned experiments:\n\n1. plan_006 - Gradient conflict analysis on v7 (3 epoch checkpoints)\n2. plan_007 - Attention heatmap visualization\n3. plan_008 - Held-out eval (status: ANALYZING)\n4. plan_009 - Llama-3.1-8B Phase 1 GAR diagnosis\n\n\n5. plan_010 - Llama-3.1-8B ThreadGate v7 training\n6. plan_011 - Llama-3.1-8B LoRA-only training\n7. plan_012 - Llama-3.1-8B 3-way eval\n8. plan_013 - Llama-3.1-8B gradient conflict analysis\n9. plan_014 - Downstream task sanity check\n\nThe \"best\" tier scenario assumes Llama-3 fully replicates the Qwen findings, the held-out eval confirms distribution shift as a cross-model structural barrier, and the original framing holds completely.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the metric ranges I'll use as anchors for my predictions—looking at the expected values for phase 1 GAR drop, training GAR, inference performance, the training-inference gap, gradient cosine similarity, magnitude ratios, and ThreadGate versus LoRA differences.\n\nFor plan_006, I have some baseline data from the paper on gradient conflict metrics, but I need to think through what the full analysis across three epoch checkpoints would show. Looking at the current status, plan_006 is still in the planning phase for gradient conflict analysis on v7, plan_007 is queued for attention heatmaps, plan_008 is actively analyzing the held-out evaluation, and there are more experiments lined up after that.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17465,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1746